From 8cf3f2fa456aad93a0a3edbfbcdc38f2ea66ce36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 23:07:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Recommendation impact testing (predictive-accuracy scope)

Final piece of Wm's July 28 roadmap item 4. Scoped July 31 (his decision)
to predictive-accuracy measurement, not true A/B impact testing: every
recommendation this generates is a SHADOW RUN, computed from real ledger
data and recorded to the chain, never acted on. True impact testing would
require wiring decide_healing_bounds/decide_queue_reordering into the
live decision path first -- a separate, much bigger product decision;
only safety_check runs live today.

decide_staffing_adjustment is deliberately excluded -- it needs real-time
agent headcount and this system has no data source for that anywhere.
Fabricating one would violate the same never-guess discipline the rest of
the codebase holds to (event_v1.py's Provenance Rule).

New ledger primitives (governance/ledger_postgres.py): two append-only
record kinds, recommendation_shadow_run and recommendation_shadow_score
(a score is always a NEW row referencing the run's hash, never a mutation
-- an append-only chain has no other way to attach a fact that wasn't
knowable until later). shadow_run_hash joins the shared canonical_fields
contract as Item 9 -- given its own dedicated column rather than reusing
replaces_hash, which already has a specific, different, fail-closed-
enforced meaning elsewhere (obligation_supersession.py). Also added
get_decisions_by_node_in_window, a real time-windowed per-queue read.

Caught mid-build and fixed: a botched edit briefly deleted a method
signature line (caught by a syntax check before it went anywhere), and
the new record kinds needed matching branches in THREE places, not one
-- the writer, PostgreSQLLedger.verify_chain()'s own explicit
reconstruction (an undocumented third site, same gotcha as ai_cost's
delivery), and twin_custody.py's recompute_current_hash (the officially
documented witness side). All three now agree.

Also found and fixed a real gap in this session's EARLIER ai_cost work:
SHIPPED_COLUMNS (twin_custody.py -- the actual list twin_shipper.py uses
to decide what reaches a twin) never had ai_cost added, so that data
would never have shipped to any twin despite hashing and verifying
correctly locally. Fixed in the same pass as adding shadow_run_hash to
the same list.

recommendation_impact.py: two shadow-run generators (healing_bounds,
queue_reordering) and two scorers, all pulling real data via
get_decisions_by_node_in_window and skipping (returning None, not
fabricating) whenever fewer than 5 real calls exist in a window. Scoring
uses a directional check (did the real outcome move toward the predicted
target relative to where it started) rather than forcing exact-value
matching, since Erlang-C-style targets are estimates, not guarantees.
Includes a CLI (run/score subcommands, --dry-run, JSON summaries) matching
obligation_sweep.py's existing CLI shape.

33 new tests: 6 ledger-level (hash/verify/refuse-unknown-hash/filtering),
12 fake-ledger unit tests for the aggregation and scoring math, 3 real-
Postgres integration tests (window filtering by node and time, and one
true end-to-end pipeline test using a real ledger, real windowed pull,
and a real fail-closed ClaudeGovernanceDecider -- same no-API-key
convention test_sentinel_worker.py already uses for real-without-network
testing). One own-test bug fixed along the way (invalid *args-with-default
syntax) and one own-test timing bug fixed (the two-window healing-bounds
pull needs genuinely time-separated data, not six rows inserted at once).

Full suite 756 passed / 6 skipped, twice back-to-back (one unrelated
throughput test flaked once under sandbox load, confirmed passing in
isolation and on a clean re-run -- test_api_server_v2.py, untouched by
this change). Ruff and bandit clean; bandit's only finding anywhere in
the touched files is the same pre-existing dev-default password at
ledger_postgres.py:115 already confirmed pre-existing in an earlier
commit this session.
